From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:40:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] build: link with the sanitizers the packages are compiled
 with

A sanitizer is a link option too: the link adds the sanitizer's runtime,
or with -fsanitize-trap leaves it out, and under LTO GCC expands the
checks only at the link, as traps or as calls into the runtime, by the
options on the link line. Packages compile with TARGET_CFLAGS, but many
link with TARGET_LDFLAGS alone, as make's built-in rule and meson do.
With CONFIG_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION holding -fsanitize=undefined
-fsanitize-trap=undefined, mtd and glib2, which use LTO, linked their
checks as calls into libubsan, which the musl toolchain does not have.

Add the sanitizer options of TARGET_CFLAGS to TARGET_LDFLAGS. A build
without sanitizers is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 include/package.mk | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/package.mk b/include/package.mk
index c71a75b..41f020b 100644
--- a/include/package.mk
+++ b/include/package.mk
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@ ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,lto,$(if $(CONFIG_USE_LTO),1,0)),1)
   TARGET_CXXFLAGS+= -flto=auto -fno-fat-lto-objects
   TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -flto=auto -fuse-linker-plugin
 endif
+# A sanitizer is a link option too: the link adds its runtime or, with
+# -fsanitize-trap, leaves it out, and under LTO expands its checks.
+TARGET_LDFLAGS+= $(filter -fsanitize%,$(TARGET_CFLAGS))
 ifdef CONFIG_USE_MOLD
   ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,mold,1),1)
     TARGET_LINKER:=mold
